WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:12.207
"I love Wednesdays!" Ally said the next morning, putting on her meld medallion.

2
00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:16.385
"It is illogical to love a day of the week," Alpha said.

3
00:00:16.386 --> 00:00:23.598
"You're right." Ally nodded. "Except I always have Wednesdays off from work.

4
00:00:23.599 --> 00:00:28.492
That's the day that Dr. Lloyd's astronomy club meets at Ray's.

5
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:32.695
The less I see him, the better!"

6
00:00:32.696 --> 00:00:37.117
"Correction," Alpha said. "That is logical."

7
00:00:37.118 --> 00:00:42.273
"You're working well today," Ally said. "I think I'll take you out with me."

8
00:00:42.274 --> 00:00:43.526
"Destination?"

9
00:00:43.527 --> 00:00:50.349
"Mateo's soccer camp. We're going to convince his coach to run an after-school soccer club."

10
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.343
"You're using your Astral mind to help others."

11
00:00:53.344 --> 00:01:04.027
Alpha almost sounded proud. "That is a very Astralian thing to do."

12
00:01:04.028 --> 00:01:09.027
*** Ally and Mateo explained their idea to Coach Cross before camp

13
00:01:09.028 --> 00:01:13.072
began. "I love this idea!" Coach Cross

14
00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:18.329
said. "I miss coaching soccer during the school year. There's only one

15
00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.906
problem." "What?" Mateo

16
00:01:20.907 --> 00:01:23.172
asked. "How will we pay for

17
00:01:23.173 --> 00:01:27.081
it? I can't charge families the same price as I charge for

18
00:01:27.082 --> 00:01:31.796
camp. And I'd like to make it accessible to all kids, so the fees will need to be

19
00:01:31.797 --> 00:01:36.430
low." "Why does everything here have to cost money?" Ally asked.

20
00:01:36.431 --> 00:01:40.972
"Where I come from, all kids' activities are free."

21
00:01:40.973 --> 00:01:44.272
"Free?" Coach Cross gave her a surprised look.

22
00:01:44.273 --> 00:01:53.270
"I wish that's how it was here too, but we have to pay rent for the field, and buy equipment like soccer balls, cones, uniforms, nets . . ."

23
00:01:53.271 --> 00:01:55.923
"How much?" Mateo asked.

24
00:01:55.924 --> 00:02:01.781
"At least five hundred dollars," Coach said.

25
00:02:01.782 --> 00:02:09.850
"That's a lot." Mateo sighed. "Where are we going to get that much money?"

26
00:02:09.851 --> 00:02:14.993
Ally remembered what the waitress at Pepe's had told her when she first arrived on Earth:

27
00:02:14.994 --> 00:02:20.736
"If you want anything in this world, you've got to work for it."

28
00:02:20.737 --> 00:02:24.540
"I guess we'll have to work for it," Ally said.

29
00:02:24.541 --> 00:02:29.177
"You're right," Mateo said. "We can plan a fundraiser."

30
00:02:29.178 --> 00:02:35.699
"Interesting idea," Coach Cross said. "What will you sell?"

31
00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:40.262
"Maybe Randy from Ray's Diner can bake cupcakes," Mateo said.

32
00:02:40.263 --> 00:02:44.056
"And we can sell them from Papi's food truck.

33
00:02:44.057 --> 00:02:46.448
That should make us a lot of money."

34
00:02:46.449 --> 00:02:50.927
"Randy's cupcakes are so good," Ally said.

35
00:02:50.928 --> 00:02:58.333
"If we charge two dollars per cupcake, we'd have to sell 250 of them," Mateo said.

36
00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:01.006
"That should be pretty easy."

37
00:03:01.007 --> 00:03:05.261
"People do love cupcakes," Coach said.

38
00:03:05.262 --> 00:03:10.179
"Uh-oh!" Ally slapped her forehead. "I just remembered something.

39
00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.667
Randy is going on vacation soon.

40
00:03:12.668 --> 00:03:19.406
We can't ask him to make that many cupcakes before he leaves."

41
00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:24.751
"Well, it was a good idea, kids," Coach said. "Thanks for trying."

42
00:03:24.752 --> 00:03:28.509
Coach started to walk away when Ally noticed his T-shirt.

43
00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:33.522
It had the name of the soccer camp and a funny picture of a soccer ball.

44
00:03:33.523 --> 00:03:38.940
"Coach! Wait a minute!" she called. "What if we sell T-shirts?

45
00:03:38.941 --> 00:03:42.850
Do people love T-shirts as much as they love cupcakes?"

46
00:03:42.851 --> 00:03:50.086
Coach's eyes lit up. "They do! My twin brother owns the Sandville Print Shop.

47
00:03:50.087 --> 00:03:54.786
I can ask him to donate the printing if we can pay for the materials."

48
00:03:54.787 --> 00:03:59.587
Coach sent his brother a text, who replied right away.

49
00:03:59.588 --> 00:04:06.534
"Eli says he's happy to help. You can go see him at the shop after camp to discuss it with him."

50
00:04:06.535 --> 00:04:10.640
"We should ask Kate to design the shirt," Mateo said.

51
00:04:10.641 --> 00:04:14.334
"She told my mom she wants to be a fashion designer one day."

52
00:04:14.335 --> 00:04:18.566
Mateo texted Kate to ask her to help with the design.

53
00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:22.834
Ally and Mateo agreed to meet up again after camp to go to the print shop. Ally

54
00:04:22.835 --> 00:04:27.870
sighed with happiness after she waved good-bye to Mateo. "I'm

55
00:04:27.871 --> 00:04:33.373
so happy I can help him before I leave!" ***

56
00:04:33.374 --> 00:04:37.005
Ally spent the morning in the park.

57
00:04:37.006 --> 00:04:41.764
On her way home, she ran into Kate.

58
00:04:41.765 --> 00:04:47.023
"I was just going to text you and Mateo some T-shirt design ideas," Kate said.

59
00:04:47.024 --> 00:04:50.423
"Here, give me your phone, and I'll upload them for you."

60
00:04:50.424 --> 00:04:57.168
Ally nervously touched Alpha in her pocket. "Kate is always asking to see Alpha," Ally thought.

61
00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:02.152
"I can't let her, especially since Alpha still isn't working right."

62
00:05:02.153 --> 00:05:08.712
"Uh . . ." The fib popped out before Ally could stop herself. "I lost my phone."

63
00:05:08.713 --> 00:05:12.894
"That's terrible!" Kate looked horrified.

64
00:05:12.895 --> 00:05:17.262
"I can't imagine being without my phone! I'll help you find it."

65
00:05:17.263 --> 00:05:21.093
"That's okay. You don't have to—" Just then Kate's phone rang.

66
00:05:21.094 --> 00:05:25.344
"It's my mom. I have to take this call, but I'll see you later, Ally.

67
00:05:25.345 --> 00:05:28.018
Don't worry, we'll find your phone."

68
00:05:28.019 --> 00:05:31.576
"No, really, please don't worry about it!" Ally said.

69
00:05:31.577 --> 00:05:38.372
But Kate had already walked off, her phone pressed to her ear.

